    overflow-y: scroll
    background-color: colors-ui-surface-base-panel
    // THE HISTORY LIST STACKS THE SAME NOTIFICATIONS AS THE LIVE TOAST STACK,
    // AND OWED THEM THE SAME GAP.
    //
    // `#active-notifications` above is `display: flex` with
    // `gap: NOTIFICATION_STACK_GAP`, so two live toasts sit 0.5rem apart. This
    // container renders the identical `.status-notification.ct-notification`
    // elements — same markup, same per-kind 0.0625rem coloured border
    // (`notifications.styl:11`) — but laid them out as plain blocks with no
    // gap and no child margin. Adjacent notifications therefore ABUTTED, and
    // two touching 1px borders read as one 2px divider rather than as two
    // separate notices; a run of same-kind notifications read as a single
    // block with lines ruled through it.
    //
    // The same token, not a new number, because these are the same objects in
    // a different place — a second value here would be the thing that drifts.
    display: flex
    flex-direction: column
    gap: NOTIFICATION_STACK_GAP
    border-top: 5px solid colors-ui-surface-primary-tertiary
    border-left: 5px solid colors-ui-surface-primary-tertiary
